{"event_type":"review","id":"f1b4ec10ce92281a420fd19658ca820137420bb9cb0ee35d03ebd6f88270e210","occurred_at":"2026-11-14T20:37:13Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/22887982b788ca6a0e9a3593f1aecb50432e593549f61115f75d0a5a3c29f085","sha256":"22887982b788ca6a0e9a3593f1aecb50432e593549f61115f75d0a5a3c29f085"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4708009f8868c0d9ff645a38392424bb95490e16e53ece7da19c1fffa37bb7e8","sha256":"4708009f8868c0d9ff645a38392424bb95490e16e53ece7da19c1fffa37bb7e8"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7fcc68035511a613d8f31f4c8fc95523ba1a5452fd1714513e5993bef907094d","sha256":"7fcc68035511a613d8f31f4c8fc95523ba1a5452fd1714513e5993bef907094d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9fed4636bd1c6cbfda7418aebabc2e2cd27a96e0652742225cf1a8438f89de6e","sha256":"9fed4636bd1c6cbfda7418aebabc2e2cd27a96e0652742225cf1a8438f89de6e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ec172d9965d1bf7454f9883121b256dfcdaf60dd4537e5b08405275d0ee60e93","sha256":"ec172d9965d1bf7454f9883121b256dfcdaf60dd4537e5b08405275d0ee60e93"}],"attempt_id":"cc23b44c6c87329094dcd1ec9de50b29ec4ba62e0acdb6fafeb62cd01d65a51f:0:1","base":"534309326e23208317be90b265eaa44b1797e7f2","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"24ee885be3f16eed87d4bdffc8f6eeb54a0dd927","body":"**Compare binary lockfiles without UTF-8 decoding.**\n\nAt `src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts`, Line 159 decodes `bun.lockb` as UTF-8, although Bun defines it as a binary lockfile. Node replaces invalid UTF-8 bytes with replacement characters, so distinct byte sequences can compare equal. For example, isolated bytes `0x80` and `0x81` both decode to the same replacement character. Compare raw buffers for lockfiles; decode only files that require parsing. ([bun.sh](https://bun.sh/docs/pm/lockfile?utm_source=openai))\n\nBased on learnings, defer this minor finding to a follow-up issue under the owner's greenfield review policy.","id":"af009564f3d50300b44d99d67e7d0420e5ece5ca9b3289dbef2cfdc713d31524","intervals":[[159,159]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Compare binary lockfiles without UTF-8 decoding."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"24ee885be3f16eed87d4bdffc8f6eeb54a0dd927","body":"**Compare workspace member lockfiles before accepting reuse.**\n\nIn `src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts`, Line 241 omits member lockfiles. pnpm supports disabling the shared workspace lockfile. In that configuration, root metadata and member manifests can remain equal while `packages/app/pnpm-lock.yaml` selects different dependency versions. This function still succeeds because it never compares that lockfile. Compare member lockfiles, or explicitly reject this configuration before accepting dependency reuse. ([pnpm.io](https://pnpm.io/10.x/workspaces))","id":"1ccc37e3507d892ba71872bf737df2b088a782b29cd52ed13d615da1a1f860b6","intervals":[[241,242]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Compare workspace member lockfiles before accepting reuse."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"4a7904f3c93e5897583d4960dcc6c7ee2b93b44e","body":"**Release temporary snapshot reservations after each attempt.**\n\n`session.bytes` increases here but never decreases for these snapshots. `releaseAddressTerminalEvidence` only releases the baseline reservation.\n\nFor nine captured 2 MiB files, the baselines reserve 18 MiB. Seven unchanged snapshots raise the counter to 32 MiB. The eighth attempt then fails the cap check, although the earlier temporary snapshots are no longer needed. If that attempt contains edits, settlement stops before it pins or restores them.\n\nRelease each temporary snapshot reservation in a `finally` block, including unchanged and failed attempts.","id":"3369423d02580886cdff387cb4183ed7859d283ab34f2e655aa1512dbd8fcb2a","intervals":[[914,915]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Release temporary snapshot reservations after each attempt."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"4a7904f3c93e5897583d4960dcc6c7ee2b93b44e","body":"**Reject every Git executable inside the checkout.**\n\nIf `PATH` contains `/checkout/..tools`, the candidate `/checkout/..tools/git` passes this check. Its relative path is `..tools/git`, which starts with `..` but remains inside the checkout. `terminalGit` can then execute repository-owned code with terminal authority.\n\nAccept an outside path only when the relative path is exactly `..`, starts with `..` plus the platform separator, or is absolute.","id":"538e0ae4da5ca2ded68dce27b6e9f4dbb93332222fac87acf8eb041e704fd96c","intervals":[[238,238]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject every Git executable inside the checkout."}],"head":"86c58f8e6884e5cf1507ad19ba6883e6b863e495","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"24ee885be3f16eed87d4bdffc8f6eeb54a0dd927","intervals":[[1,244]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressDependencies.ts"},{"blob":"4a7904f3c93e5897583d4960dcc6c7ee2b93b44e","intervals":[[1,1093]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts"},{"blob":"23627ab10088d83ce3a03797b0fe743083e46be0","intervals":[[1,1014]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressManyPlan.ts"},{"blob":"5144753a32c1edd87a8802b2bb453b417b017987","intervals":[[1,99]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/localReview.ts"},{"blob":"75396bfe557fc2c95f918e17a64ba64124a5959b","intervals":[[1,540]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/reviewOperation.ts"}],"job_id":"cc23b44c6c8